Jonadab the Unsightly One <jonadab.theunsightlyone@gmail.com> wrote:
> Currently, if you die in Sokoban, your game is not eligible
> to leave bones.  I think I understand why the developers
> made this choice, but ...

Many people have criticized Sokoban's design[1] and said it doesn't
really fit into the game. I'm not one of the Sokoban haters but I too
think it's not perfect.

Disallowing bones is a logical workaround for a level where there's
only one true way to solve it and every other creative solution will
be punished. Which is completely contrary to the rest of the game.


If you'd like to have bones in Sokoban, I think there would be a
simple solution to it.

Remove the luck penalties from Sokoban and replace them with a
solved-Sokoban-correctly tracking and enable bones for the Sokoban
levels.

This would neatly solve it without lots of special code.


[1] For example, Derek Ray is on record for wanting to throw Sokoban
    out of SporkHack completely because of various reasons but not
    doing it because he had no suitable replacement.

